      "name": null,
      "problem": "Find the set of values of $x$ that satisfy $2<2x+4\\le 6$ and $4x>12.$",
      "worked_solution": "To solve compound \"and\" inequalities, we solve each inequality separately and then find their intersection.\n\n- First, we solve $2<2x+4\\le 6\\,:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2 & <2x+4\\le 6 \\\\ 2-4 & <2x+4-4\\le 6-4 \\\\ -2 & <2x\\le 2 \\\\ \\frac{-2}{2} & <\\frac{2x}{2}\\le \\frac{2}{2} \\\\ -1 & <x\\le 1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14224662/assets/485e77fe84f5745120d5f450c3e1043ee61463a83f7c12bfc6d1ae0e4124a38b.png)\n\n   \n\n- Then, we solve  $4x>12\\,:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4x & >12 \\\\ \\frac{4x}{4} & >\\frac{12}{4} \\\\ x & >3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14224662/assets/654f97a64ec1a13b4a94860dfa07d05f7c119a5fe2084ba23aa994a97f0bea70.png)\n\nTo find the values of $x$ that satisfy both inequalities, we find where the two solutions overlap:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14224662/assets/d2d0f41792356b6c250612b033413f66bfd7a35440e1b84da660fccd5c1285b0.png)\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nIt turns out that the solutions do not overlap at all. Therefore, there are no values of $x$ that satisfy both inequalities simultaneously. So, there is no solution.",
